        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4e6b3b59-7067-5eb7-9f08-306c726978e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Tarawa, Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River, Second Phase Campaign Western Sector\n- Organizations: Eighth Army Ranger Company\n- People: Ralph Puckett Jr.\n- Places: Ch'ongch'on River Valley, North Korea, Tifton, Georgia\n- Topics: Korean War, Pacific Theater of World War II\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Tarawa was fought in the Pacific Theater of World War II from 20 to 23 November 1943.\n- The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River, also called the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on or the Second Phase Campaign Western Sector, took place during the Korean War from 25 November to 2 December 1950.\n- The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River was fought along the Ch'ongch'on River Valley in northwestern North Korea.\n- Ralph Puckett Jr. was born on 8 December 1926 in Tifton, Georgia.\n- Ralph Puckett Jr. led the Eighth Army Ranger Company during the Korean War.\n- The Eighth Army Ranger Company was best known for defending Hill 205 against a Chinese attack during the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River.\n- The defense of Hill 205 during the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River resulted in 41 of the 51 Rangers becoming casualties.\n- The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River was a decisive battle in the Korean War.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f2489891-eaf4-5f95-a94e-23240c5f72d8",
        "text": "Page: Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River. Sentence: The Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River, also known as the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on () or the Second Phase Campaign Western Sector (), was a decisive battle in the Korean War, and it took place from November 25 to December 2, 1950, along the Ch'ongch'on River Valley in the northwestern part of North Korea.\nPage: Battle of Tarawa. Sentence: The Battle of Tarawa was a battle in the Pacific Theater of World War II that was fought on 20–23 November 1943.\nPage: Eighth Army Ranger Company. Sentence: It was best known for its defense of Hill 205 against an overwhelming Chinese attack during the Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River which resulted 41 of the 51 Rangers becoming casualties.\nPage: Ralph Puckett. Sentence: Ralph Puckett Jr. (born 8 December 1926 in Tifton, Georgia) led the Eighth Army Ranger Company during the Korean War.",
